                                "sense_id": "37ee24ad-ce59-3374-ad4a-8c14cd045abc",
                                "text": "\"Bursting with poetic allusions and Scudder’s intricately wrought drawings that illustrated every stage of butterfly life — eggs and larvae, shapes and forms — these volumes, Nabokov later wrote, “inaugurated a new era in lepidopterology.'\""
                            },
